            <div xml:id="d786">

                <pb facs="0842" n="738" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg738"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/5132: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-04-30T16:00:00-04:00">April 30, 1932—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>162. For the Minister. Your April 28, 9 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Your purpose, as indicated in paragraph 9 of your April 28, 9 p.m., has
                        the Department’s approval provided the representatives of the other
                        participating friendly powers make similar designations.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>When informed that the agreement has been signed, the Department will give
                        consideration to the question of your return to Peiping mentioned in
                        paragraph 10 of your telegram.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
